Building the OMNeT++ documentation
==================================

The documentation is built only in the doc-builder container image
(https://github.com/omnetpp/doc-builder), which has the whole toolchain: Sphinx
with the OMNeT++ extensions, doxygen, graphviz, pandoc and TeX Live. The image is
pinned by digest in doc-builder.image. build.sh runs a target of the Makefile in
it, with podman or docker; the Makefile refuses to run outside the image.

The unified HTML site (manual, guides, tutorials, articles, C++ and Python API
reference) and the PDFs it links to:

    $ ./build.sh ci-html

A live preview of the site at http://localhost:8000/:

    $ ./build.sh site-server

The outputs of the release archives (doxygen API references, the HTML, PDF and
Eclipse-help manual and guides), also built by `make doc` in the OMNeT++ root:

    $ ./build.sh all

See build.sh for the variables it takes (VERSION, WHAT, BUILDID, BASEURL, IMAGE,
ENGINE). The site build/deploy pipeline is documented in site/README.md.
